  "as_of_notes": "Figures are from the official 'Statewide Registered and Enrolled Data File (Active Status)' dated 3/7/2026 ('After Inactivation Process'). This is ACTIVE-status registrations only; inactive-status voters are published in a separate file. The published Excel file totals 897,677 active registered voters statewide and is internally consistent (county sums and party sums both reconcile exactly to the grand total).",
  "data_quality": "high \u2014 official SoS Excel data file parsed directly; all 16 counties present; statewide party sum and county total sum both reconcile exactly to 897,677.",
  "notes": "Source provides voting-district / municipality-level granularity; aggregated here to county level for all 16 counties. Maine registers by party (enrollment). Active-status party columns in the file: D=Democratic, R=Republican, U=Unenrolled, G=Green Independent, L=Libertarian. 'Other' in this schema = Libertarian (5,680). No 'No Labels' column appears in this snapshot (No Labels is not an active qualified party in this file). Inactive-status registrations are excluded (separate file). The SoS news page also cited ~1,038,603 active voters as of 1/1/2026 under a different/earlier compilation; this JSON uses the most recent published data file (3/7/2026 Active, after inactivation)."
